cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
title: "The first missed move at factor 400 in the 547/727 prime race"
abstract: "The first 400H miss in the dyadic 547/727 prime-ideal race is a gain, at a starting height located to within a factor of 1.0131. This holds whenever eight primitive Dirichlet L-functions have no zeros in an explicit bounded region, a condition supplied by the announced Dirichlet GRH theorem. Failure of this localization unconditionally forces a zero in the specified region."
